Apache License, Version 2.0 or the MIT license, at your option.

The MapLibre Native FFI project modified that software. Changes against
upstream `v/0.6.2` (commit 1099f161bfc5e3ac7f90aad88b1bf788e72906cb):

- `android/rustls-platform-verifier/src/main/java/org/rustls/platformverifier/CertificateVerifier.kt`
  moved to the `org.maplibre.nativeffi.internal.rustlsplatformverifier` package so
  it can coexist with the upstream helper, and dropped its additional
  `PKIXRevocationChecker` pass so Android's trust-manager policy decides
  revocation.
- `rustls-platform-verifier/src/verification/android.rs` and
  `rustls-platform-verifier/src/tests/ffi.rs` point their JNI class descriptors
  and exported symbol names at the package above.
- `android/rustls-platform-verifier/build.gradle`,
  `android/rustls-platform-verifier/proguard-rules.pro`,
  `android/rustls-platform-verifier/src/androidTest/java/org/rustls/platformverifier/CertificateVerifierTests.kt`,
  and `README.md` follow the same package rename.

The complete modifications are published as patch files under
`patches/rustls-platform-verifier/` in the MapLibre Native FFI source
repository (https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi).
